{# Best Practices #}
<section class="ss-c-demo__section">
    <h2>Best Practices</h2>

    <div class="ss-l-grid ss-l-grid-auto">
        <div class="ss-c-card">
            <h3>✓ Use semantic names</h3>
            <p>Always use the <code>z()</code> function with meaningful layer names. Never hardcode z-index values.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ss-c-card">
            <h3>✓ Respect the hierarchy</h3>
            <p>Follow the layer order: canvas → content → interface → modal → guides. Don't skip layers without
                reason.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ss-c-card">
            <h3>✓ Use offsets sparingly</h3>
            <p>When you need relative stacking, use small offsets (+1 to +10). If you need larger gaps, consider
                adding
                a custom layer.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ss-c-card">
            <h3>✓ Document custom layers</h3>
            <p>If you add custom layers to <code>$layer_map</code>, document their purpose and position in the
                stack.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ss-c-card">
            <h3>✗ Avoid z-index: 9999</h3>
            <p>The "make it bigger" approach leads to unmaintainable code. Use the layer system instead.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="ss-c-card">
            <h3>✗ Don't create stacking context chaos</h3>
            <p>Remember that <code>position: relative/absolute/fixed</code> with z-index creates new stacking
                contexts.
                Plan accordingly.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
